Users re-type the same filters every day. Let them save a search and rerun it from the board.

AC-1: A saved search persists its name and filter.
AC-2: Saving a name that exists replaces it.
AC-3: Running a saved search returns the same rows as typing the filter.
AC-4: A missing name returns a clear error.
AC-5: `factory search save <name> <filter>` stores a search.
AC-6: `factory search run <name>` prints the rows.
AC-7: `factory search list` prints the names.
AC-8: `factory search rm <name>` removes one.
AC-9: Every command prints a one-line error for a missing name.
